  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing low-cost age-friendly community (AFC) initiatives focusing on the built environment through Voice capacity strengthening and small grants for community engagement using an intergenerational approach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal: To disseminate the key messages of the Let&apos;s Go guide through Voice workshops with OPAs and youth groups at the community level in up to 5 pilot countries, with a view to piloting a process that could potentially be scaled up across more countries (or more communities within the same countries) via joint fundraising for larger scale AFCs voice work. To give sustainability and support to the work already completed in the region in the first phase, the next steps would seek pilot countries preferably selected from countries where the grants supported by AARP were used, eg Colombia, Per&#xFA;, Dominican Republic, Chile, Argentina, Costa Rica, Brazil.</narrative>
  </description>
